Z||000006||theogre||01-25-2001||07:40 PM||||Yes, you can just disconnect the bat for a few seconds to rest the ECM.<P>The fuel regulator is a pain to work on with a 300 series TBI. If you suspect problems there you need to hook up a fuel pressure gauge and run the tests in the various books. Low pressure could be either the FP reg or the pump in the tank. high pressure could be the reg or a blocked return line.<P>Unplug the relay and see if the idle settles. Only reason I can think it would effect idle is if the relay was pulling allot of juice but it would also be likely to get really hot if that was the case. If the idle seems to be effected by diferant electrical things on the car I'd start checking all the ground ties after having the charging system checked.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
